.TH HZJPG 1 "November 2026" "hzjpg 1.0" "User commands"
.SH NAME
hzjpg \- bit-exact lossless repacking of baseline JPEG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hzjpg pack
< image.jpg > image.nvj
.br
.B hzjpg unpack
< image.nvj > image.jpg
.SH DESCRIPTION
A JPEG is DCT coefficients entropy-coded with Huffman, and Huffman cannot
code a symbol in less than one bit.
.B hzjpg
decodes the Huffman stream and recodes the SAME coefficients with an
adaptive arithmetic coder whose contexts are the neighbouring blocks and
the neighbouring slots. The pixels are never touched: this recodes the
entropy layer, not the image.
.PP
The proof is in the packing: before anything is written, the coefficients
are encoded back to Huffman and compared byte for byte with the original.
On any difference the exit status is 2 and the caller stores the file raw.
.PP
Baseline sequential JPEG only (SOF0/SOF1). Progressive and
arithmetic-coded JPEG exit with status 2.
.PP
The old subcommand names
.BR packa " and " packaupp
remain as aliases.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 usage error, 2 cannot transform this file (expected for
progressive JPEG \(em not an error).
.SH HISTORY
Born as nvjpg; renamed hzjpg on 2026-11-20. The stream format and its
magic are unchanged \(em every stream the old tool wrote, this one reads.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hz (1)
